count. You can cancel or pause online at any time.", "A Kids profile can ask for a book that isn't on its shelf; a grown-up says yes or no in Account → Family with the account password, and a yes opens that one book for that profile.", "A grown-up can give a Kids profile a bedtime in its profile editor, with the account password: from 7pm to 10pm, and when reading starts again in the morning. Between them, on that device's clock, books and audiobooks show Time for bed and the place is saved; the password allows 15 more minutes.", "Grown-up and teen profiles can put a book on the family shelf from its page; it shows on Home for everyone at home, and Kids profiles see only the books their rating already allows.", "Each LiteraryWorm title's page has Content notes, written by AI: how much violence, death, frightening scenes, language, sexual content, alcohol and drugs, prejudice and self-harm it has, without spoilers. Grown-ups see them under a Kids profile's book requests too. They can miss things, so check anything that matters to you."]}, {"heading": "Book clubs and buddy reads", "paragraphs": ["On a book club's page, Where everyone is shows the chapter each member has reached, for members who turn on Show my place to this club; it's off until you turn it on.", "Under a club's discussion, Shared highlights shows passages members marked in the book; ones from chapters you haven't reached stay hidden until you choose to see them. Share one of yours from the list there, with or without its note, and stop sharing it whenever you like.", "A club can read a LiteraryWorm title or a book you uploaded, such as a DRM-free EPUB you bought. When you start a club in My Library → Clubs, choose LiteraryWorm books or My uploads under Book from, then find the book by title, author or ISBN (an ISBN is looked up on Google Books and matched by title and author), or choose Keywords under Search by to look through descriptions and genres too.", "Sort the list by title, author, numbers first or series in reading order, and filter it to one series.", "Uploads stay private, so members don't get your file. The club shows the book's title and author, and each member uploads their own copy and chooses it on the club's page (Choose your copy). Posts, where everyone is and shared highlights then follow each member's place in their own copy, so nothing past their chapter is spoiled. An uploaded book has no recording, so there's no listening along.", "To read a book with one friend, choose Read with a friend on its page. A buddy read is a book club for two: send your friend its code, and you get spoiler-safe posts by chapter, meetings and shared highlights."]}, {"heading": "Your plan, notifications and gifts", "paragraphs": ["Your plan includes some hours of audiobooks a month for the household (Premium has no limit) and a number of devices that can keep books offline. Account → Plan and billing shows how much you've used this month and which devices hold offline places, and lets you free one.", "To hear when a book you set Remind me on comes out, turn on Notifications on this device in Account → Preferences. Once it's on, choose there which notifications you get: books you're waiting for, club meetings, new club posts up to your chapter, an evening streak nudge, and answers to Kids book requests. On iPhone and iPad, add LiteraryWorm to your Home Screen first (Share, then Add to Home Screen) and turn them on in the app.", "When you buy a gift on Gifts, you can add up to 10 LiteraryWorm books to it (find a title, or add one of your lists); they're waiting in the recipient's library when they redeem it."]}, {"heading": "Logging in and keeping your account safe", "paragraphs": ["In Account → Sign-in you can add a passkey to log in with your face, fingerprint, screen lock or a security key instead of your password, and rename or remove passkeys you no longer use."]}, {"heading": "Trouble logging in?", "paragraphs": ["If Log in or Log in with a passkey does nothing, check that your browser isn't letting LiteraryWorm access your local network. LiteraryWorm never needs that permission, and allowing it can stop logging in from working. In Chrome and Edge, select the icon beside the address, choose Site settings, set Local network access to Block, then reload the page and log in again. If your browser asks whether LiteraryWorm can find devices on your local network, choose Block.", "Still stuck? Try a private or incognito window. If that works, a browser extension or something saved in your usual window is in the way. Otherwise, email support@literaryworm.com with your device and browser."]}, {"heading": "Report a problem", "paragraphs": ["Tell us what you were doing, the page you were on, and your device and browser, by email to support@literaryworm.com.", "For accessibility problems, email accessibility@literaryworm.com. To report a post, an upload or a copyright problem, email report@literaryworm.com. For privacy questions, email usprivacy@literaryworm.com."]}]$lw$::jsonb;

update public.changelog_entries set body = $lw$My Library → Uploads can now search your EPUBs by ISBN too: Google Books says which book it is, and your uploads with that title and author show. When you start a club, Find a book and Find one of your uploads take a title, author, keywords or ISBN in one box: keywords also look through LiteraryWorm books' descriptions and genres, and your uploads' part names.$lw$
where title = $lw$Find uploads by ISBN, and club books by keywords$lw$ and version = '2026.11' and body = $lw$My Library → Uploads can now search your EPUBs by ISBN too: Google Books says which book it is, and your uploads with that title and author show. When you start a club, Search by now offers Keywords beside title, author or ISBN, for Find a book and Find one of your uploads: LiteraryWorm books are searched by description and genres too, uploads by their part names.$lw$;

